    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46432" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωθήκη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small room wherein to rest by
			day</i>, opp. <i>dormitorium</i> (the bedroom), <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2.17.21
			</span></i>; <i>zothecula</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.6.38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>niche</i> in a wall, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				145.1
			</span></i> (pl.); used as a <i>chapel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Supp.Epigr.
				2.849
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Alexandria</span>); Lat.<i>zotheca</i>,
			Dessau <i><span class="en">
				<u>ILS</u>
				5449
			</span></i>, al.</div>
